{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/537762-thoughts-on-a-belial-s-brood-initiation","id":537762,"title":"Thoughts on a Belial's Brood Initiation?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-02T22:34:22-07:00","id":537762,"title":"Thoughts on a Belial's Brood Initiation?","content":"Hi! I am often a lurker here, just made it official to ask a question on a project I have going. We have a Brood covey and are doing and initiation rite. I need ideas for the three sections of the initiation: Submission, Ordeal, Conundrum.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Submission: which is actually representing the ability to submit to your own Beast which is a very Brood thing.<br /> <br /> Ordeal: <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">frightening and terrifying, it's purpose s to induce the altered state of consciousness.<br /> <br /> Conundrum: </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">a dilemma that must be resolved, competently, by a savage hand.</span></span><br /> <br /> Does anyone have any ideas? We'd like this to be pretty challenging and graphic and memorable. Rated R (or X) is fine. If the idea isn't appropriate for this forum you can message me privately of course, I don't want to offend anyone but this is the Brood and it's pretty edgy by nature.<br /> <br /> Killing of ghouls, touchstones, fire, sunlight, taking of limbs, eyes, tongues, swallowing things -- all fair game. Be evil, but thoughtful, and creative. Evil should have a strategy and a purpose.<br /> <br /> Thanks so much for the help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6242-nickcave","name":"nickcave","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T10:48:48-07:00","id":538539,"title":"","content":"The Belial's Brood book goes a long, long way towards adding depth to them, including how one becomes a member. I can fully appreciate not wanting to get another book just for one game, but I'll explain it, briefly, before offering ideas relating to your own question. The entire journey is called the Pursuit, and it is divided into three stages like your own idea. First there's the Call, which is when a vampire feels that they don't fit into vampire society, and basically come to the realization that, whatever trappings their covenants offer and excuses and reasons, it's not enough and the vampire feels they're living a lie. At this point they either directly meet with another member of the Brood, or begin seeking a Resonant. The idea is that they need a little help in reaching the Adversary, and so they seek out an inanimate object, ranging from tomes to dolls to murder implements or even once-holy relics, but now corrupted by some deep emotion or act that gets it 'in tune' with the Adversary. I suppose in second edition terms, it would have a Resonance. Lastly is Cathexis, which is where the vampire's soul, in touch with the Vitae of another Brood mate or a Resonant, fully connects with the Adversary. There's one last choice they can make there, whether to go through with it or leave the whole idea behind, and it's entirely up to the vampire to make.<br /> <br /> I love Belial's Brood, they're a great faction.<br /> <br /> Anyways, in terms of Submission, I'd suggest murder-via-frenzy followed by diablerie. Frenzy is arguably the core of the vampire experience, and it certainly submits to the Beast, while diablerie is, arguably, the pinnacle of the vampire experience, where one is not merely feeding on Blood or Vitae, but drinking the very soul of another Kindred.<br /> <br /> I suppose if you wanted to continue with that into the Ordeal, you could either have a point where the 'killed' vampire's soul lingers within the initiate, urging them to self destruction at every turn, whispering doubts and doing all it can to free itself by causing the initiate to destroy themselves. An alternative would possibly be a sort of meditation. <a href=\"http://www.vice.com/read/ten-days-of-silence-taught-me-how-to-be-alive-500\" target=\"_blank\">I read an article the other day about this place that puts people through extreme meditation.</a> A variant of that might be interesting, perhaps staying up for 10 nights and 10 days without feasting until even the ravenous, starving Beast inside is silenced so that a vampire can hear their 'true' self. Perhaps you tie in both, so that a vampire has to fully appreciate the devouring of the soul as it rails against its enforced silence until it eventually dies, engulfed in the heart of the initiate.<br /> <br /> From there is the Conundrum. There's something to be said for the killing of, or destruction of in the case of inanimate, touchstones. A lot of things, really, but one of them could easily be, 'I am no longer that person.' An initiate doesn't want something to anchor their humanity. They have a new purpose, though they might have to decide what that is, whether it is becoming a demon incarnate or serving the Adversary directly, they have to figure out something that keeps them, even at Humanity 1 or 0, from becoming a mindless draugr, and instead allows them to continue their path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T17:45:00-07:00","id":538965,"title":"","content":"That's incredibly insightful, thank you!<br /> <br /> Because this is happening in an actual game, i'd have to find an actual PC to have the initiate kill/diablerize... and while that is certainly on the table for the Brood, it's a big 'first step' for a young group. I want to make sure it really has some behind it when we pull out that big gun -- PKing someone is pretty harsh. But I love this. It's much more thoughtful than I expected. Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6242-nickcave","name":"nickcave","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T19:47:04-07:00","id":539116,"title":"","content":"Cool! Glad you liked it, happy I could help out. I really like having the Brood in my games, and when they do things they can be very harsh but it's a fitting darkness for the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T08:01:43-07:00","id":554292,"title":"","content":"As an aside, does it affect much Belial Brood's creed and concepts the fact that humanity now serves different standards and colaterals, so to speak?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T10:20:01-07:00","id":554540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/537762-thoughts-on-a-belial-s-brood-initiation?p=554292#post554292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an aside, does it affect much Belial Brood's creed and concepts the fact that humanity now serves different standards and colaterals, so to speak?</div> </div> </div> </div> If you're talking about 2e? Not really. <br /> <br /> A large part of the Brood is &quot;dark enlightenment,&quot; and communion with the Beast. If the Invictus, Lance, and Ordo made up the three Estates that are focused on controlling the Beast, then the Carthians, Crone, and Brood focus on being parners with it. The Brood embodied a kind of opposite-Ordo Dracul. <br /> <br /> Its more difficult to pull off Brood 2e in part because the Ordo Dracul itself has moved from being all about controlling the Banes into something more akin to making all aspects of the vampirism better, and the other part because a good chunk of the story of the Brood is tied to being a Lance-style heresy. <br /> <br /> What's left of the Brood's niche is to be vampires that move closer in mind and body to the strix themselves.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T06:50:38-07:00","id":555583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/537762-thoughts-on-a-belial-s-brood-initiation?p=554540#post554540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you're talking about 2e? Not really.<br /> <br /> A large part of the Brood is &quot;dark enlightenment,&quot; and communion with the Beast. If the Invictus, Lance, and Ordo made up the three Estates that are focused on controlling the Beast, then the Carthians, Crone, and Brood focus on being parners with it. The Brood embodied a kind of opposite-Ordo Dracul.<br /> <br /> Its more difficult to pull off Brood 2e in part because the Ordo Dracul itself has moved from being all about controlling the Banes into something more akin to making all aspects of the vampirism better, and the other part because a good chunk of the story of the Brood is tied to being a Lance-style heresy.<br /> <br /> What's left of the Brood's niche is to be vampires that move closer in mind and body to the strix themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, i meant in 2e, sorry for the lack of clarity.<br /> <br /> So, even thought the outlook on humanity per se changed, the leashing/unleashing the Beast stays mostly the same.<br /> Good to know and the additional info clears up a bunch of stuff too. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}